          "case_name": "In re Child of Barni A.",
          "citation": "2024 ME 16",
          "court": "Supreme Judicial Court of Maine",
          "year": 2024,
          "date_decided": "2024-01-31",
          "holding": "The Law Court vacated termination of a mother's rights to her medically fragile child and remanded, holding that where the Department never provided the 24/7 private duty nursing to which the child was legally entitled under MaineCare and never followed up on indications that the mother has an intellectual disability, the record did not establish her unfitness by clear and convincing evidence.",
          "relevance": "The case turns on the child's entitlement to Level IV Private Duty Nursing under MaineCare and the Department's failure, as the program administrator, to supply it.",
          "quote": "We cannot assume that the mother would have been found unfit if the Department had met its legal obligations.",
          "url": "https://www.courtlistener.com/opinion/9471586/in-re-child-of-barni-a/",
          "courtlistener_cluster_id": 9471586
        },
        {
          "case_name": "Cunningham v. Haza",
          "citation": "538 A.2d 265 (Me. 1988)",
          "court": "Supreme Judicial Court of Maine",
          "year": 1988,
          "date_decided": "1988-02-29",
          "holding": "The Law Court vacated judgment on the pleadings for a child protective caseworker, holding that where the complaint alleges she interviewed and physically examined a child at school without parental notice, acted beyond her statutory authority, and acted with malice, Maine Tort Claims Act immunity could not be resolved on the pleadings.",
          "relevance": "The caseworker's physical examination of the child during a school interview is the conduct the Court held could fall outside her statutory authority.",
          "quote": "At a minimum, however, plaintiffs' complaint alleges that defendant acted beyond the bounds of any statutory authority she might have, and that she acted with malice.",
          "url": "https://www.courtlistener.com/opinion/1926300/cunningham-v-haza/",
          "courtlistener_cluster_id": 1926300
        }
